Certain cuneiform signs were used as shorthand for entire words, like how "7"
is short for "seven", or "&" short for "and". These signs are written in
CAPITALS to make it clear that they're not conveying the actual Hittite
pronunciation.

> ilan carrahhun
Nu ḫilamnaš luttāi šarraḫḫun.

Nu=za=kan ḫilamni anda ešun.

Nu apiya āškan Ù luttāi ōḫḫun.
Nu GIŠ^ḫattalu āški ēšta.

Verbs: ōḫḫun, pāun, šarraḫḫun, dāḫḫun, tēḫḫun, katta tēḫḫun
             <2> iškiši            
