Most of the sentences you've seen so far have only one noun, but this doesn't
have to be the case. To put one thing into or onto another, for example, you'll
need both an accusative noun and a dative noun.

> nu dankui paun
Nu pēdan kuit dankui ēšta, parā natta taruḫḫun pāun.

> agannic dahhun
"Aganniš" is likely a scribal error; this is a valid noun, but the nominative
case doesn't make sense in this context.

> agannin dahhun
Nu DUG^agannin natta taruḫḫun dāḫḫun. Nu paḫḫur änza ēšta.

> pahhur dahhun
Nu paḫḫur natta taruḫḫun dāḫḫun. Nu paḫḫur änza ēšta.

> hattalu hacci tehhun
Nu GIŠ^ḫattalu ḫašši tēḫḫun. Nu GIŠ^ḫattalu lukket.

Nu=za=kan É^arkiwi anda ešun.

Nu apiya ḫaššan Ù šuppandan LÚ^ḫalliyatallan ōḫḫun.
Nu paḫḫur Ù DUG^aganniš ḫašši anda ešer.

Nu warān GIŠ^ḫattalu ḫarkun.

